# pabetoop-league — project-local ignores

# ── dependencies & build output ──────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
/bin/
dist/

# ── runtime state (regenerated; never commit) ────────────────────────────────
data/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# ── scratch space ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `tmp/*` rather than `tmp/` so the acceptance harnesses can be tracked: a
# whole-directory exclusion cannot be re-included from, and the docs cite these
# scripts as the way to run a gate. A fresh clone needs them. The re-include is
# `*.sh`, not a name prefix, so a harness called anything else is still tracked —
# a doc citing an uncommitted script is a gate nobody can run.
tmp/*
!tmp/*.sh

# ── client build artefacts ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The bundled htmx build IS tracked (offline-first); everything else compiled is not.
web/static/js/app.js
web/static/js/app.js.map
